WEBVTT

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:15.200
I... um... You see, I work as an idol...

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.920
There's something I'd like to ask
a legendary detective to handle!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.630
Hate to say it, but I'm no detective...

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.800
Then--

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.050
Sorry.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.060
This unmotivated-looking
guy is only a sidekick.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.270
But it's okay.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.270
If it's a detective you want,
there's one right here.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.570
I'm the legendary detective
Nagisa Natsunagi.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:51.280
The detective is already dead...
but her dying wish will never die.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.500
Episode 3

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.920
My name is Yui Saikawa.
I work as an idol.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.800
Yui Saikawa?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.260
So, you see... the thing is...

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.720
I want you to prevent a sapphire
with a market value of three billion yen

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.260
from being stolen before it happens!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.510
What happened was,

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.060
last month, a warning, giving advance
notice of the crime, arrived!

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.850
We strengthened our vault security
measures, but on the appointed day,

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.480
the security personnel will be
at my live performance venue--

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.480
Whoa, calm down. That's a good girl...

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.320
Let's relax a little, okay?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.280
This week's...

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.910
...idol news!

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.740
This week we're looking at that
middle school idol who can sing and dance,

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.540
and commands the tip-top of all
the hit charts, Yui Saikawa-<i>san</i>!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:26.680
Yui Saikawa's live tour starts next week

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.040
So cute!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:13.010
Since her debut as a sixth grader,
with her unique songs and dance style,

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.970
her adorable expressions have won her
popularity with fans of all ages.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.970
The live tour of the world's
cutest idol, Yui Saikawa-<i>san</i>...

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:22.810
Oh!

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:23.720
...at last...

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.770
Next week!

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.060
...will begin!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.560
Yay!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.150
Are you... the real thing?

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:35.150
Ouch! Hey! Don't run away!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:40.950
Why'd you do that all of a sudden?
Don't you know who I am?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.870
I'm the world's cutest idol, Yui Saikawa!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.620
Who do you think you are,
treating <i>me </i>like that?

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.460
Calm down, Saikawa.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.500
The saliva of the world's cutest idol is
now smeared all over both my hands, sure,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.710
but I'm not going to be enjoying
myself later by collecting it

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.840
with a cotton swab
to keep or anything like that.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.390
Eww! I thought you were a detective,
but you're a pervert!

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:05.680
Wait, are you the criminal
who sent that warning?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.020
Eeek! Somebody call... call the police!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.900
Hate to tell you, but the police
and I have a really tight relationship.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.320
Th-That's awful! Are you saying this whole
nation is hopelessly corrupt--

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.110
from bottom to top?

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:24.410
The police, the lawyers, the politicians
are all on the side of a panty thief?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.330
Hold on just a minute. Stop lumping
together being a pervert with theft

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.920
to try to make me out as a panty thief!

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.340
To be clear, I'm neither
a pervert nor a thief!

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.420
Uh-uh, you deserve 2,000 years
for the crime of pervertedness.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.970
That's absurd. I'm not a bad person.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.550
That's what every criminal says.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:49.850
Sorry, we've got a lot going on today;
could we talk details tomorrow?

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:55.520
Oh, I see... Well, if you say so,
Ms. Detective, we'll have to go with that.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.440
Okay, I'll see you tomorrow! Absolutely!

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:05.950
You really intend to work as a detective?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:11.830
Yeah. Somehow, my body was already
in motion by the time I realized it.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:17.090
In Natsunagi's presence, I'm trying
to keep my cool to the utmost, but...

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:20.220
The former partner who
I'd thought had died...

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:26.680
What's more, only her heart is alive,
and beating right before my eyes...

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.810
With that fact alone, my brain's already
working at 100% capacity;

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.610
I didn't have the head space
to read much into any of this.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.740
Sure, I'd have just been laughed
at by my former partner

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:43.570
for saying such sentimental stuff...

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.030
You could've at least said
goodbye before you died...

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:52.790
Or is that why you came back?
To say goodbye? Or was it...?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.420
Kimizuka.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.840
No, it's just...

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.930
Looking forward to working with you.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.840
Oh... yeah.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.720
Well, I'm heading home.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.060
Right. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.350
"City Bus"

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.690
Once I became aware of it,

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:18.980
it felt as though I'd been searching
for someone for a long time,

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.440
but in reality, it was only
for about this past year...

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.530
Or should I say, I think
the thing I call an identity

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.040
was also only established
very recently.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:35.370
During my childhood, I was always ill,
spending all my days in bed...

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.340
I wanted to put on running shoes
and sprint around a track.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:43.630
I wanted to take detours and
goof off with friends after school.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.260
But none of those wishes would come true.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.390
If I couldn't get things even
when I wished for them,

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:52.310
I thought I was better off
not wishing in the first place.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.190
So I didn't really need a self-image.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:59.650
Or rather, I most likely
avoided having one.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.700
But one day, a wish came that
I desperately wanted to fulfill.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:12.120
This heart was crying out. It was crying
that there was someone it wanted to see.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.410
I suddenly realized I'd started running.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:21.380
You're the legendary detective?

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:25.380
The source of hope I thought I'd finally
found was listless, without spirit,

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:29.970
and looked as though he'd already
given up on a lot of things.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.770
Something about him
looked like the old me.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:37.690
So I couldn't leave him be.
I flew off the handle at him,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.610
even inadvertently let him see me cry.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.030
That... That was a blunder...

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:46.490
Natsunagi... whomever
that heart may belong to,

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:50.160
you can live your own life.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:08:03.710
He said those words just for me. So my
life begins again, fresh--here, today.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:11.300
Umm, ahem. I apologize
for getting upset yesterday.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:19.650
Before we get to that... just how long
is this table? We're way too far away!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:23.520
Oh, really? I don't think it's that big!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.070
Then why have we been shouting
at each other this whole time?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:28.950
Well, that's obvious.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.870
If we spoke normally, we wouldn't
be able to hear each other!

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:36.660
Doesn't that mean there's
something off about your house?

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.790
Okay, so to re-focus...

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.090
By the way, that left eye--is it injured?

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.840
Oh, this is--how do I put it--
a "playing a character" kind of thing.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.760
Idols have a tough struggle
to survive, too.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.510
Sorry to call you here
on such short notice.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.350
It's just that time is
already running short.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.100
It's fine.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:04.060
You can leave all your worries to me,
Nagisa Natsunagi, legendary detective!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.900
Where is all this confidence coming from?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.490
Now, Saikawa-<i>san</i>,
could you tell us the details?

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:15.740
Yes. What happened was,
the other day, this arrived.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.200
A letter?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:23.040
"On the day of Yui Saikawa's
live performance at the Dome,

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.590
we will take possession of the
sapphire valued at three billion yen."

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:27.960
So in this day and age,

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.590
there are thieves conscientious enough
to send a notification like this.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.140
I want you to prevent that
before it happens.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.180
I see. And do you know what this
"three-billion-yen sapphire" refers to?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.310
Yes, I think it's unmistakably

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.770
the "Miracle Sapphire,"
a family heirloom kept in the vault.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.440
But if you know the date of the crime,

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.070
isn't it better to just increase security
on that particular day?

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:53.360
You've got a large number of
security personnel in this house.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.950
No, that's just it--that's not possible,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.620
because on the day of the crime,
I have a live performance.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:04.500
Ah... You mean they'll serve as security
detail at the performance venue?

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.580
Uhh... no.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:10.710
They're my biggest fans, so to them,
guarding a three-billion-yen sapphire

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:14.430
isn't as important as watching
my song-and-dance performance.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.420
"Yui Saikawa"

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.180
You all need to find different jobs!

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:20.100
Seriously. If you're just going to mess
with us, excuse me, but I'm leaving.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.270
Wait, Kimizuka.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:27.400
Since she specifically placed her trust
in us, can't you listen a little longer?

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.780
What's up? You're being awfully insistent.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:34.200
Come on, an assignment from a girl
who lives in this kind of house?

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.570
That means...

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:40.450
You may be right, but detective isn't a
profession to pursue just for the money.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.500
With that said,
money <i>is </i>a necessity, right?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:48.670
That is certain. After experiencing three
years of traveling as vagabonds,

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:52.130
I believe I comprehend better than
anyone the importance of money.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.670
You're reading yourself
for eventualities like--

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.260
A new swimsuit...

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.720
Oh.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:01.640
Well, even if we have different goals,
money still definitely matters.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.020
So... is that it?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:07.770
On the day of the show, Natsunagi and
I just need to guard your home vault?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.730
Yes. That's basically it.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:13.990
In that case, isn't it better
to leave it to the police?

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.450
I discussed it with them once,

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.910
but with only the threat letter,
they wouldn't deal with it.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:26.580
Hey, that face--like, "Why not dangle
some money to motivate the police?"

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.080
That's just the way a pervert would think.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.210
I haven't said any such thing yet!
Still, that's just what I was thinking.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.260
Certainly, my way of thinking is,

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:39.390
"If you don't have pastries,
just purchase a bakery."

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:43.600
That's a thought process that would've
stunned even Marie Antoinette...

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.060
So that's the deal.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:50.360
Umm, why are you the one
who's requesting this, Yui?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.400
If a Saikawa family heirloom
is being targeted for theft,

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.780
why not your father or mother?

00:11:56.780 --> 00:12:00.370
My parents died three years ago.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.870
So the head of the Saikawa household...

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.870
...is me!

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:11.920
This... is the Saikawa family heirloom,
the Miracle Sapphire.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.840
It's huge. Not her style at all, though.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.590
Amazing... It's beautiful!

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.970
We do have an airtight
security system in place...

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.890
Hurry up and go use the restroom.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.230
Eh? Eww, how did you know?

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:33.070
You truly have exceptional
pervert powers of observation.

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:35.030
An ordinary person could never fake that.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.820
A certain someone trained me that way.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.320
I may have drunk too much tea.
Excuse me for a minute.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.620
Some detective.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.880
Kimizuka-<i>san</i>...

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.000
Wha--?

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.460
Now I see.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:13:00.430
You feel pleasure when someone breathes
in your ear--you're that type of pervert.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:04.050
Stop making me out as a pervert
with your contrived interpretations.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.180
Hey, what's this?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.640
This is a photo from my first live show.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.270
It's a super-rare picture that hasn't
ever even been posted online.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.610
Are you starting to become
obsessed with me after all?

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.610
Have you become a fan?
Are you in love with me?

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:25.160
But I'm sorry. I'm an idol,
so falling in love is out of the question.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.200
Look me up in the next life.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.540
Quit taking it upon yourself to profess
<i>my </i>feelings and then to turn me down.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.250
More importantly--she's still not back?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.460
Quite a stunning beauty, eh?

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.470
Sure, as far as looks go. Her personality
leaves something to be desired, though.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:42.470
Oh, Natsunagi-<i>san </i>is, too, but I meant me.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.220
You have no hesitation about singing
your own praises, do you?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.810
That's right; in the world of idols,

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.730
it's hard to get by without
this level of self-confidence.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.070
Having outfits sliced apart by rivals,
or having tacks stuck in your shoes

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:58.530
are an everyday occurrence.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:04.570
But I hear that such rivals all vanish
from the center stage the next day.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.410
That's a coincidence...
Has to be a coincidence, right?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.920
I like you, Kimizuka-<i>san</i>. Your reactions
are funny. It's a joke--just a joke!

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.670
Which parts are the joke,
and which aren't...?

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:19.380
The part where I said
I like you was the joke.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:24.220
Ah, okay, now I get it.
You're messing with me.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.180
No, that last part was the real joke.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:33.730
I can't get a grasp on when you're
putting me on and when you're for real.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:37.400
Being an idol is a deeply
toilsome profession.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.610
Not much sense asking now,
but are you doing all right with all this?

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.740
Eh? With all what?

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:48.080
Sunday is your live stadium show, right?
But with that letter having shown up...

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:50.080
Just the... How do I put it?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:55.080
Mentally, you might say...
isn't it too much to shoulder all alone?

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.800
I'm all right. I'm not all alone.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.390
You're kind, Kimizuka-<i>san</i>.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:10.010
Kind? Not many people
have said that to me.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:15.770
It might be that you're starting to grow
the heart of a human being.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.980
Stop treating me like some
robot living with a scientist

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.820
who has learned to feel emotions.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:24.070
You <i>are </i>funny, Kimizuka-<i>san</i>.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.530
Give me a little more of
a look around this room.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.620
Go ahead--feel free.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.120
This looks like it could turn into
more trouble than I imagined.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.170
So how about this case?
Think we can handle it?

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.420
Will you get mad if I say this is
different from what I expected?

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:46.590
Why would I?

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:50.100
You say that,
but detective work is hard.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:55.310
I thought it would be more like looking
for runaway cats and that kind of thing.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:59.900
You need to immediately apologize
to every single detective in the nation.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.570
Yesterday...

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:08.070
...I had a dream. With Siesta-<i>san</i>.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:11.530
Really... Did she seem
to be doing all right?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.240
For starters, I was intimidated
by how amazingly pretty she was.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.120
Right?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.290
Well, I'm not sure what it means
that you're so proud of that, but...

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.960
Did you talk to her about anything?

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.590
Yeah... we had a big blowout argument.

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:26.970
You shouldn't have blowout arguments in
a dream with a person you've never met...

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.680
...but still, I kind of get it.

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:33.180
We went at it verbally without holding
back, and she wasn't backing down,

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.770
but in the end, she told me
to do with you as I saw fit.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:43.770
So I was the cause of the fight...

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:48.280
N-No! It's not like
we were fighting over you.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.490
What's with that reaction?
That makes it even worse.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.540
Aargh, we're done talking about this!

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:56.910
The gist is, she said we should
just do our best together--

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.290
with me as detective, and you as sidekick!

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.880
Sure, sure. A new swimsuit
is at stake, right?

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.050
You want to see me in
a bikini, too, don't you?

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:08.630
Yeah, totally...
I must see, right this moment.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.840
That apathy is irritating.
But that's all right.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.470
It is?

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:17.890
Okay, if we can safely resolve this case,
you want to go to the beach with me?

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.560
Do you have a death wish or something?

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.520
I'm not going to die.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:31.240
I won't die. To voluntarily die
and leave you on your own...

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.080
...I'd never do that.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.830
I see.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.670
Hurry up, Natsunagi!
The rehearsal is about to start.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.920
Umm, just what is all that?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.720
"All that," what?

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:53.390
That!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.090
Yui is Life

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:54.670
Love Yui

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.630
Sa

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:00.770
What have you been doing this whole week?

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:03.480
You haven't come to school,
and when I tried to contact you,

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.730
you never replied.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.320
When I finally did get a reply,

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:08.730
it said we were going to a rehearsal
the day before the show.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:13.070
No, it's just, as I was binge-watching
Yui-<i>nya</i>'s past TV appearances,

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.910
before I knew it, it was already today...

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.490
Yui-<i>nya</i>?

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.790
That's what all her fans call her.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.460
Okay... I'm gonna murder
you multiple times.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:25.920
I give... give up.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.050
Do you understand what tomorrow is?

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:30.590
It's Yui-<i>nya</i>'s live show.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:35.050
It's that, too, but that's not
what most concerns us, right?

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.390
We have to protect the Miracle Sapphire
from that crook. Am I wrong?

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:40.310
I understand what you're
saying, Natsunagi,

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.020
but there's also a grasp
of the true situation

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.020
that comes into view by learning
about the client's background, right?

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.360
Well, maybe. But even so,
would that normally go as far

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:50.940
as begging Saikawa-<i>san</i>
to go watch a rehearsal?

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.900
Once you accept a job, you go all in.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:57.410
And also, tomorrow we have
to guard Yui-<i>nya</i>'s house,

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.370
so we need to have all
the fun we can today.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.620
You just admitted this is about the fun.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.040
I'll bet her opening number is
gonna be "Raspberry Grizzly"...

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.090
I'm telling you: I don't know anything
about the order of her set list!

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.550
Come on, the rehearsal's gonna start!

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:15.880
♬ The express train of love
can't make any stops ♬

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.680
Hoo-hoo!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:21.220
♬ Wait for me at the last station ♬

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:22.680
Fuwa-fuwa!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:26.690
♬ I'm leaving behind the train
that stops at every station ♬

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.690
Don't leave us!

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:30.270
♬ We don't allow breakdowns
on the Nine-Star! ♬

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.360
Yeah!

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.700
Is he for real?

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:37.030
Thank you so much!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:41.990
That was "Sudden Stop on the Nine-Star
Express" from my second album!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.200
Oh, so it <i>does </i>stop.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.540
Don't sweat the little things.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.960
Now for my next song...

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:48.750
Here it comes.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.040
Here what comes?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:54.510
Come on, Natsunagi. "Eight-one" is coming.
That means the next song is...

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:56.880
I told you, I have no idea
about the set list.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:00.760
And don't abbreviate "Sudden Stop on
the Nine-Star Express" to "Eight-One"!

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:14.100
Nine times nine equals eighty-one...
cut it out with your geeky thinking!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.550
Nine-Star Express sudden stop Kyuuteisha]

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.760
Nine [kyuu]                                kyuu

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.440
Oh, nice deduction, legendary detective.
Next will be Yui-<i>nya</i>'s show-stopper.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.770
This is what we really came
to hear, isn't it?

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.860
Did we? That's news to me.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:17.240
You don't know it? This song's big hook
reveals what Yui-<i>nya </i>has sealed up inside.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.240
Sealed up?

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:23.120
Yeah, sealed up. Yui Saikawa's secret.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:27.750
Here it is... "Sapphire Phantasm"!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.250
Ah, that was great.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:36.470
Saikawa-<i>san </i>truly is a pro...

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:37.760
Huh?

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:42.100
Hey, Kimizuka, isn't there
something off about that guy?

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.470
Eh? Is something wrong?

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.110
Hey, who is that guy? Grab him!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.030
So it was...

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:58.650
Kimizuka! Quick!

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.740
As a person, she's lovely to behold;

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:07.620
for a detective, though,
those extreme emotions are of no use.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:14.250
Kindness, compassion--even those can
sometimes come back to bite you.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:17.630
Natsunagi doesn't realize that yet.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.510
Are you all right?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.060
Oh, Mr. Pervert!

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:28.350
Even in these circumstances?
Stop calling me a pervert.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:31.770
I mean, if you're joking around,
hey, don't let me stop you.

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:34.820
However, what may happen is unclear.

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:37.320
Security for the vault tomorrow matters,

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:41.320
but you should tighten up
this stadium's security as well.

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:43.700
Show me around the backstage
area of this hall later.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:45.410
I will.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.370
The principles governing the actions
of this breed called the detective

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:54.040
all come down to logic...

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.800
Can you stand?

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:59.880
Yes. Thank you.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:01.590
However...

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.930
That means that when the question
at hand unequivocally changes,

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:07.560
there are truths that come to light.

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:10.890
That's right. Yui Saikawa...

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:14.560
...is lying.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
Episode 4

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
What I See in That Eye
